      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-27y+21z &=-39 \\\\ 8x-72y+56z &=-104 \\\\ x-9y+7z &=-13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -27 & 21 & -39 \\\\ 8 & -72 & 56 & -104 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 7 & -13\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_3\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & 7 & -13 \\\\ 8 & -72 & 56 & -104 \\\\ 3 & -27 & 21 & -39\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-8)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & 7 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -27 & 21 & -39\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-3)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -9 & 7 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
